# <%= @title %>

Generated with `izen new`. A lightweight [Roda](https://roda.jeremyevans.net/)
app on top of the Izen core (SQLite, no ORM, no autoloader).

## Setup

```sh
bundle install
cp .env.example .env
bundle exec izen migration migrate
bundle exec izen dev
```

`izen dev` boots the Rack/Puma development server on port 3000. Pass
`--port PORT` / `--host HOST` to change the bind address.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `app.rb` | Roda application (routes live here) |
| `app/` | Domain modules (`model`, `contract`, `repository`, `controller`, colocated views) |
| `app/layout.erb` | Shared ERB layout |
| `migrations/` | Versioned up/down SQL migrations |
| `config/database.yaml` | SQLite path per `APP_ENV` |
| `config/storage.yml` | Upload storage service per `APP_ENV` (default: `local`) |
| `storage/` | SQLite databases, the session secret and uploaded files |
| `config/deploy.yml` | Kamal deploy config for CRuby (git-ignored) |
| `config/deploy.native.yml` | Kamal deploy config for the native binary (tracked) |
| `Dockerfile.native` | Image build for the native binary (tracked) |
| `.kamal/` | Kamal secrets (git-ignored) |
| `native/` | Generated Spinel native project (`izen native build`) |

## Adding a module

```sh
bundle exec izen module new post title:string body:text
bundle exec izen migration migrate
```

## Tests

```sh
bundle exec rake test
```

## Deploy (Kamal)

`izen new` scaffolds `config/deploy.yml` (CRuby), `config/deploy.native.yml`
(native) and `.kamal/secrets-common` for a [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org)
deploy. Fill in the placeholder server, host and image, export the secrets, then
build and ship the native binary:

```sh
bundle exec izen native pack
export SESSION_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
export APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
bundle exec izen native kamal setup       # first time
bundle exec izen native deploy            # afterwards
```

`izen native deploy` runs `kamal -c config/deploy.native.yml deploy`; its
arguments are deploy options (`-d staging`, `--skip-push`, ...). Use
`bundle exec izen native kamal <args>` for any other Kamal command (e.g.
`izen native kamal setup`, `izen native kamal app logs`).

`izen native pack` lowers the app to a [Spinel](https://github.com/matz/spinel)
project in `native/` — one native binary, no interpreter, no Rack, no Puma — and
writes `pack/`, which the image builds from. The
native image is built from the tracked `Dockerfile.native` at the project root,
with `native/` (holding `pack/`) as the build context; `config/deploy.native.yml`
pins both. The SQLite database and the session secret live on the
`<%= @name %>_native_storage` volume mounted at `/app/storage`, so redeploys keep
their data.

To run a second native environment (say staging) with its own host, image and
volume, add `config/deploy.native.staging.yml` and deploy with
`bundle exec izen native deploy -d staging`.

`config/deploy.yml` (CRuby) and `.kamal/` are git-ignored locally: they hold
server details and secrets. `config/deploy.native.yml` and `Dockerfile.native`
are tracked templates — the actual secrets stay in `.kamal/secrets-common`.
